          "w": 190.0
        },
        {
          "cost": 0.0,
          "documentation": "William handles intake and Internet approval/contact/modification/cancellation. Patrick and Robert prepare, bake and pack. Jack, Paul, Richard and Harry plan/deliver and settle delivered orders. Counter and pickup settlement is assigned to William. Unknown Counter Prepare actors are retained, not filled from adjacent events. In the global view this is a shared information concept for every applicable branch; a representative association is drawn to keep the diagram readable.",
          "duration": 0.0,
          "h": 150.0,
          "id": 118,
          "kind": "TextAnnotation",
          "name": "* Roles inferred from tasks. People are observed. 5 business events have no actor.",
          "pos": {
            "x": 270.0,
            "y": 805.0
          },
          "w": 340.0
        },
        {
          "cost": 0.0,
          "documentation": "Prepare -> Bake -> Pack repeats one to three times in the logs. The model generalizes this as a loop; no defect/rework cause or one-cycle/one-sale equivalence is asserted. Cash and Give order occur in both orders. Logical parallel routing expresses that flexibility, not simultaneous human work. Branch labels are explanatory, not an executable decision engine. In the global view this is a shared information concept for every applicable branch; a representative association is drawn to keep the diagram readable.",
          "duration": 0.0,
          "h": 150.0,
          "id": 120,
          "kind": "TextAnnotation",
          "name": "Loops and order flexibility are observed; their business cause and timing are unknown.",
          "pos": {
            "x": 270.0,
            "y": 1555.0
          },
          "w": 340.0
        },
